xvfb: run the fake vblank at the rate a client asks for, on a precise timer

A client that waits for the fake vblank of a screen without a driver of its
own -- a Vulkan or GL client presenting FIFO, a compositor that paces itself
on Present -- draws at that vblank's rate, so the rate follows what a client
sets and the cadence keeps microseconds.

- A client sets _FAKE_SCREEN_FPS (CARDINAL, 1 to 1000) on the root window,
  and the screen runs at the faster of that rate and the one it started at
  (-fakescreenfps, 60 by default); deleting the property returns it to the
  start rate. The MSC stays continuous across a change, and vblanks already
  queued are retimed at once.
- One timerfd serves the queue, armed for its soonest vblank to the
  microsecond, so a rate whose interval is not a whole millisecond keeps an
  even cadence.

